{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-act-5-1","title":"Acts 5:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 After that Ananias and Sapphira his wife for their hypocrisy, at Peter's rebuke had fallen down dead; 12 and that the rest of the apostles had wrought many miracles; 14 to the increase of the faith; 17 the apostles are again imprisoned; 19 but delivered by an angel bidding them preach openly to all; 21 when, after their teaching accordingly in the temple, 29 and before the council, 33 they are in danger to be killed; but through the advice of Gamaliel, a great counsellor among the Jews, they are kept alive, and are only beaten; 41 for which they glorify God, and cease no day from preaching.</p>\n<p>Cir. A.M. 4038. A.D. 34. Le 10:1-3; Jos 6:1; Mt 13:47,48; Joh 6:37; 2Ti 2:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-5-2","title":"Acts 5:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>kept. Jos 7:11,12; 2Ki 5:21-25; Mal 1:14; 3:8,9; Joh 12:6; 1Ti 6:10 2Pe 2:14,15 his. 9 laid. 4:34,35,37; Mt 6:2,3; 23:5; Php 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-5-3","title":"Acts 5:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>why. Ge 3:13-17; 1Ki 22:21,22; 1Ch 21:1-3; Mt 4:3-11; 13:19; Lu 22:3 Joh 13:2,27; Eph 6:11-16; Jas 4:7; 1Pe 5:8; Re 12:9-11 lie to. or, deceive. 9; Job 22:13; Ps 94:7-9; Isa 29:15; Jer 23:24; Ho 11:12 to keep. Nu 30:2; De 23:21; Pr 20:25; Ec 5:4; Ro 2:21,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-5-4","title":"Acts 5:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>was it not thine. Ex 35:21,22,29; 1Ch 29:3,5,9,17; 1Co 8:8; 9:5-17; Phm 1:14 why. 8:21,22; Jos 7:25,26; Job 15:35; Ps 7:14; Isa 59:4; Eze 38:10; *marg: Jas 1:15 thou hast. 3; Ex 16:8; Nu 16:11; 1Sa 8:7; 2Ki